& [WhyNow] is supported by completed prerequisites
  + [core] is deterministic signed query and inspection passed
  + [prepared_runtime] is immutable generation replacement and concurrent snapshot execution passed
  + [self_hosting] is a real governed SOP corpus compiled and queried through CLI and MCP
  + [measurement] is prepared repeated reads are approximately two orders of magnitude below direct reload-and-admit queries
  + [operator_need] is share one verified generation and activate replacements without restarting every caller

& [WhyThisShape] is the least authority-expanding service
  + [loopback] avoids remote exposure while retaining cross-platform local client support
  + [explicit_config] preserves the no-listener-by-default requirement
  + [token_file] avoids command-line secret disclosure
  + [activation_descriptor] separates operator publication from model requests
  + [monotonic_compare] prevents stale or replayed activation
  + [core_delegation] prevents adapter semantic drift
  + [one_request_per_connection] bounds state and simplifies failure recovery

& [Alternatives] records rejected options
  + [restart_per_query] is correct but cannot share prepared state or atomic refresh
  + [automatic_file_watch] obscures activation causation and is deferred
  + [HTTP_framework] adds premature surface and dependency weight
  + [non_loopback_TCP] violates the local-only boundary
  + [request_selected_path] lets untrusted callers steer runtime authority
  + [service_compilation] collapses candidate building and trusted activation

& [SecurityReview] is fail closed
  + [secret] is fixed-length token content excluded from all outputs
  + [path] is canonical root-contained environment activation
  + [transport] is loopback-only with frame, connection, and timeout bounds
  + [state] is complete immutable generation snapshots
  + [failure] is typed and bounded without silent fallback

& [ImplementationBoundary] is safe Rust
  + [crate] is cantor_service with cantord and cantorctl binaries
  + [core_change] is only shared environment preflight and runtime snapshot support when necessary
  + [rollback] is retain direct cantor CLI and standalone cantor-mcp
  - never: treat successful daemon startup as semantic admission proof without complete core preflight
